    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. The complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 90 degrees. Therefore, the complement of \\( x \\) is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. This relationship can be expressed with the following equation:\n\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, let's solve this equation step by step:\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to isolate the variable on one side:\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Combine like terms:\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n4. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\n5. Simplify:\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nThus, the degree measure of the angle is \\( \\boxed{60} \\) degrees.",
