    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's first define what an angle's measure is. The measure of an angle is the amount of rotation from one side to another. In this case, we are given that the measure of an angle is double the measure of its complement. Let's call the angle's measure \\( x \\) degrees.\n\nThe complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the original angle, results in 90 degrees. So, the complement of the angle \\( x \\) is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\n\\( x = 2(90 - x) \\)\n\nNow, let's solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\( x = 180 - 2x \\)\n\n\\( 3x = 180 \\)\n\n\\( x = 60 \\)\n\nSo, the degree measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees.",
