      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of complementary angles. Two angles are complementary if their measures add up to 90 degrees. Let's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. Then, the measure of its complement would be \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the angle is double the measure of its complement. So, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, let's solve this equation step by step:\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to isolate the variable \\( x \\):\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees.",
